   "sec": "cause-ind",
   "html": "<p><b>Blackbook — Pre-hepatic (unconjugated hyperbilirubinemia)</b></p><h4>Increased Production</h4><ul><li>Hemolysis</li><li>Ineffective Erythropoiesis</li><li>Hematoma</li></ul><h4>Decreased Hepatic Uptake</h4><ul><li>Sepsis</li><li>Drugs (eg. Rifampin)</li></ul><h4>Decreased Conjugation</h4><ul><li>Gilbert’s Syndrome</li><li>Crigler-Najjar Syndromes (I and II)</li></ul>"
  },
  {
   "op": "append",
   "sec": "cause-dir",
   "html": "<p><b>Blackbook — Conjugated hyperbilirubinemia</b></p><h4>Hepatic (see Elevated Liver Enzymes scheme)</h4><ul><li>Hepatocellular</li><li>Cholestatic</li><li>Dubin Johnson</li></ul><h4>Post-Hepatic — usually has duct dilatation on ultrasound: Biliary Duct Compression</h4><ul><li>Malignancy</li><li>Metastases</li><li>Pancreatitis</li></ul><h4>Post-Hepatic — Intraductal Obstruction</h4><ul><li>Gallstones</li><li>Biliary Stricture</li><li>Cholangiocarcinoma</li><li>Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis</li></ul>"
  },
